Subject: wifi7: retain shared-band LEDs and expose command failures

Count every active interface on a band so closing one BSS cannot turn off
the LED shared with another running BSS. Keep the existing chip GPIO map
and make mapping queue failures and MCU command failures observable.
Validate LED arguments against their wire widths and use the selected
mapping entry directly. Size the unified 1s/2s PWM commands correctly and
reject unsupported formats before allocating or appending a command.

